9.3 Writing out \(\underline{\underline{\kappa}}\,\underline{d} = \underline{F}\)

\[
\begin{bmatrix}
\int_0^L N_{0,x}N_{0,x}\,dx & \int_0^L N_{0,x}N_{1,x}\,dx & \int_0^L N_{0,x}N_{2,x}\,dx \\[4pt]
\int_0^L N_{1,x}N_{0,x}\,dx & \int_0^L N_{1,x}N_{1,x}\,dx & \int_0^L N_{1,x}N_{2,x}\,dx \\[4pt]
\int_0^L N_{2,x}N_{0,x}\,dx & \int_0^L N_{2,x}N_{1,x}\,dx & \int_0^L N_{2,x}N_{2,x}\,dx
\end{bmatrix}
\begin{bmatrix} d_0 \\ d_1 \\ d_2 \end{bmatrix}
=
\begin{bmatrix} F_0 \\ F_1 \\ F_2 \end{bmatrix}
\]


\[
\begin{aligned}
F_0 &= \int_0^L N_0 f\,dx + N_0(0)h - g\int_0^L N_{0,x}N_{3,x}\,dx \\[4pt]
F_1 &= \int_0^L N_1 f\,dx - g\int_0^L N_{1,x}N_{3,x}\,dx \\[4pt]
F_2 &= \int_0^L N_2 f\,dx - g\int_0^L N_{2,x}N_{3,x}\,dx
\end{aligned}
\]

9.4 Simplifying based on the supports of the functions

\(N_0\) and \(N_2\) are not adjacent — their supports (elements 0–1 and 1–2 respectively) share at most a single point, so \(\int_\Omega N_{0,x}N_{2,x}\,d\Omega = 0\). The same holds for \(N_0\)/\(N_3\) and \(N_1\)/\(N_3\). This is the origin of sparsity: most entries of \(K_{AB}\) vanish because most pairs of basis functions don’t overlap.


\[
\begin{bmatrix}
\int_0^L N_{0,x}N_{0,x}\,dx & \int_0^L N_{0,x}N_{1,x}\,dx & 0 \\[4pt]
\int_0^L N_{1,x}N_{0,x}\,dx & \int_0^L N_{1,x}N_{1,x}\,dx & \int_0^L N_{1,x}N_{2,x}\,dx \\[4pt]
0 & \int_0^L N_{2,x}N_{1,x}\,dx & \int_0^L N_{2,x}N_{2,x}\,dx
\end{bmatrix}
\begin{bmatrix} d_0 \\ d_1 \\ d_2 \end{bmatrix}
=
\begin{bmatrix} F_0 \\ F_1 \\ F_2 \end{bmatrix}
\]


\[
\begin{aligned}
F_0 &= \int_0^L N_0 f\,dx + h \\[4pt]
F_1 &= \int_0^L N_1 f\,dx \\[4pt]
F_2 &= \int_0^L N_2 f\,dx - g\int_0^L N_{2,x}N_{3,x}\,dx
\end{aligned}
\]

10.1 The element stiffness matrix
On element \(e\), of length \(\ell_e = x_1^e - x_0^e\), the two local functions and their derivatives are

\[
\begin{aligned}
N_0^e(x) &= \frac{x_1^e - x}{\ell_e}, &\qquad N_1^e(x) &= \frac{x - x_0^e}{\ell_e}, \\[6pt]
N_{0,x}^e &= -\frac{1}{\ell_e}, &\qquad N_{1,x}^e &= +\frac{1}{\ell_e} .
\end{aligned}
\]

The four local integrals \(\int_{x_0^e}^{x_1^e} N_{s,x}^e N_{t,x}^e\,dx\) are then four constants times \(\ell_e\), and they fit in one small matrix:

\[
\underline{\underline{k}}^e =
\begin{bmatrix}
\left(-\frac{1}{\ell_e}\right)^{2}\ell_e & \left(-\frac{1}{\ell_e}\right)\left(\frac{1}{\ell_e}\right)\ell_e \\[6pt]
\left(\frac{1}{\ell_e}\right)\left(-\frac{1}{\ell_e}\right)\ell_e & \left(\frac{1}{\ell_e}\right)^{2}\ell_e
\end{bmatrix}
= \frac{1}{\ell_e}
\begin{bmatrix} 1 & -1 \\ -1 & 1 \end{bmatrix}
\]


Every element of every mesh of this kind has that same matrix; only \(\ell_e\) changes. Adding each \(\underline{\underline{k}}^e\) into the rows and columns of its own two nodes rebuilds the global matrix, one element at a time — assembly, which Class 10 takes up with the IEN array.

\[
\frac{\partial x}{\partial\xi} = \sum_a x_a^e \frac{\partial N_a(\xi)}{\partial\xi}
\qquad\qquad \text{if } N_a \text{ is the $a$-th Lagrange basis function}
\]

B.9 Explore the strong form
Move the sliders and watch each line of the strong form act on the solution. The black curve is the exact \(u(x)\). A blue dot marks each Dirichlet face, and the dashed amber line is the slope that the Neumann condition forces on its face. The band below the curve is the wall, shaded by temperature, with arrows showing the heat flux \(q = -\kappa u_{,x}\).

viewof hBC = Inputs.radio(new Map([
  ["(a) Hughes: h at x = 0, g at x = L", "a"],
  ["(b) swapped: g at x = 0, h at x = L", "b"],
  ["(c) g at both faces", "c"]
]), {value: "a", label: "Boundary conditions"})
viewof hF  = Inputs.range([-2000, 2000], {value: 500, step: 50,  label: "f (W/m³)"})
viewof hH  = Inputs.range([-300, 300],   {value: 50,  step: 5,   label: "h (W/m², into wall)"})
viewof hG  = Inputs.range([0, 40],       {value: 20,  step: 1,   label: "g (°C)"})
viewof hG0 = Inputs.range([0, 40],       {value: 35,  step: 1,   label: "g at x = 0 in (c) (°C)"})
viewof hK  = Inputs.range([0.2, 5],      {value: 1.4, step: 0.1, label: "κ (W/(m·K))"})












































heat = {
  const L = 0.30, k = hK, f = hF, h = hH, g = hG, g0 = hG0;
  let u, du;
  if (hBC === "a") {
    u  = x =&gt; g + h / k * (L - x) + f / (2 * k) * (L * L - x * x);
    du = x =&gt; -h / k - f * x / k;
  } else if (hBC === "b") {
    u  = x =&gt; g + (h + f * L) / k * x - f / (2 * k) * x * x;
    du = x =&gt; (h + f * L) / k - f * x / k;
  } else {
    u  = x =&gt; g0 + (g - g0) * x / L + f / (2 * k) * x * (L - x);
    du = x =&gt; (g - g0) / L + f * (L - 2 * x) / (2 * k);
  }
  const q = x =&gt; -k * du(x);
  const pts = d3.range(121).map(i =&gt; { const x = L * i / 120; return {x, u: u(x), q: q(x)}; });
  return {L, k, f, h, g, g0, u, du, q, pts};
}







{
  const {L, u, du, q, pts} = heat;
  const W = Math.min(width, 760);
  const dirX = hBC === "a" ? [L] : hBC === "b" ? [0] : [0, L];
  const neuX = hBC === "a" ? 0 : hBC === "b" ? L : null;
  const marks = [
    Plot.line(pts, {x: "x", y: "u", stroke: "#1a1a1a", strokeWidth: 2.6}),
    Plot.dot(dirX.map(x =&gt; ({x, u: u(x)})), {x: "x", y: "u", r: 6, fill: "#1e3a5f"})
  ];
  if (neuX !== null) {
    const d = (neuX === 0 ? 1 : -1) * 0.08;
    marks.push(Plot.line([{x: neuX, u: u(neuX)}, {x: neuX + d, u: u(neuX) + du(neuX) * d}],
      {x: "x", y: "u", stroke: "#d97706", strokeWidth: 2.4, strokeDasharray: "7,4"}));
  }
  const top = Plot.plot({
    width: W, height: 300, marginLeft: 55,
    x: {label: "x (m) →", domain: [0, L]},
    y: {label: "↑ temperature u (°C)", grid: true},
    marks
  });

  // the wall, shaded by temperature, with flux arrows
  const segs = pts.slice(0, -1).map((p, i) =&gt; ({x1: p.x, x2: pts[i + 1].x, u: p.u}));
  const qmax = d3.max(pts, p =&gt; Math.abs(p.q)) || 1;
  const nA = 7, cell = L / nA;
  const arrows = d3.range(nA).map(i =&gt; {
    const x = cell * (i + 0.5), len = 0.8 * cell * Math.abs(q(x)) / qmax, s = Math.sign(q(x));
    return {x1: x - s * len / 2, x2: x + s * len / 2, y: 0.5};
  }).filter(a =&gt; Math.abs(a.x2 - a.x1) &gt; 1e-4);
  const band = Plot.plot({
    width: W, height: 110, marginLeft: 55,
    x: {label: "x (m) →", domain: [0, L]},
    y: {axis: null, domain: [0, 1]},
    color: {type: "linear", scheme: "RdYlBu", reverse: true, legend: true, label: "u (°C)"},
    marks: [
      Plot.rect(segs, {x1: "x1", x2: "x2", y1: 0, y2: 1, fill: "u", stroke: "u"}),
      Plot.arrow(arrows, {x1: "x1", x2: "x2", y1: "y", y2: "y", stroke: "#1a1a1a",
                          strokeWidth: 2.4, headLength: 10})
    ]
  });
  return html`&lt;div&gt;${top}${band}&lt;/div&gt;`;
}







